<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Higo Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Higo Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a>, corresponding to modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumamoto-prefecture">Kumamoto Prefecture</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kato-kiyomasa">Katō Kiyomasa</a> received its northern half in 1588 and the whole province after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Battle of Sekigahara</a> in 1600, and from 1632 it was held by the Hosokawa clan as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumamoto">Kumamoto</a> domain until 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/higo-province.jpg" alt="Higo Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Higo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
